libv4l2: publish devices_used under the open mutex

v4l2_fd_open() claims a free slot in devices[] under v4l2_open_mutex, but
grows devices_used - the bound v4l2_get_index() searches up to - only
later, after the unlock. Two opens running at once race on it: if the one
that got the higher index writes first and the one with the lower index
writes last, devices_used shrinks and the higher slot falls outside the
search.

That device still looks open. Its QUERYCAP succeeded, since that ran
through the plugin inside v4l2_fd_open() itself. But every later ioctl on
the fd is looked up, not found, and passed to the kernel on the plugin's
dummy file instead - so the first control the application sets fails with
EINVAL and nothing in the plugin ever sees it.

ustreamer opens its H.264 encoder and its JPEG encoders from separate
threads at the same moment, through two libv4l-rkmpp instances. About one
start in twenty lost one of them this way: "Can't set option
V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_BITRATE: Invalid argument", then "Encoder destroyed due
an error (prepare)", and no WebRTC (or one JPEG worker) until the streamer
next restarted.

Grow devices_used inside the critical section that claims the slot, so it
can only increase.

--- a/lib/libv4l2/libv4l2.c
+++ b/lib/libv4l2/libv4l2.c
@@ -732,6 +732,16 @@
 			devices[index].plugin_library = plugin_library;
 			devices[index].dev_ops_priv = dev_ops_priv;
 			devices[index].dev_ops = dev_ops;
+			/*
+			 * Publish the slot under the same lock that claimed
+			 * it. Updated after the unlock, two concurrent opens
+			 * race on devices_used: the one holding the lower
+			 * index can write it last and shrink it, and the
+			 * other device drops out of v4l2_get_index() - its
+			 * ioctls then bypass the plugin entirely.
+			 */
+			if (index >= devices_used)
+				devices_used = index + 1;
 			break;
 		}
 	}
@@ -779,9 +789,6 @@
 	devices[index].readbuf = NULL;
 	devices[index].readbuf_size = 0;
 
-	if (index >= devices_used)
-		devices_used = index + 1;
-
 	/* Note we always tell v4lconvert to optimize src fmt selection for
 	   our default fps, the only exception is the app explicitly selecting
 	   a frame rate using the S_PARM ioctl after a S_FMT */
